{
	title: 'Motion timed by frequency',
	spec: 'Each direction of a UI change is timed by how often it happens (user request 2026-10-12, loosening Emil Kowalski): a frequent or keyboard-driven change takes 50 ms (3 frames at 60 Hz; web --snap-ms), its rare reverse fades back over 300 ms (--back-ms, --ease-out). The state itself changes at once; only its look animates. Web motion is CSS; script it only when CSS cannot. Under prefers-reduced-motion, fades and color changes stay and movement goes. Applied to the prompt: typing erases the example from its left within 50 ms in total, on both clients (placeholders.follow); when the box empties again the example fades back in over 300 ms: on the web by CSS, in the terminal by color steps from the box background on 50 ms frames (quartic ease-out, close to --ease-out) where ansi.fades(), else at once. The example shown first on opening does not fade. Composer buttons: Send and the others turn on in 50 ms and off in 300 ms (color and the 40% contents fade); Nudge the other way round. Mobile Nudge slides behind Send in 50 ms and fades back over 300 ms ease-out (replacing 250 ms and 500 ms ease-in-out); under reduced motion it fades without sliding. Hover backgrounds keep 120 ms. skills/ui-craft has a Motion section based on Emil Kowalski skills with this rule; tasks/README.md Motion (web) states it.',
